                                "name": "British Columbia"
                            },
                            "location": {
                                "lat": 49.2827291,
                                "lng": -123.1207375
                            },
                            "rent_stats_latest": {
                                "year": 2026,
                                "month": 1,
                                "data": [1814.0, 1689.0, 1330.0, 2119.0, 2362.0, 3279.0, 3838.0, 4453.0, 2650.0, 0.3, -1.2, 0.7, -1.5, 1.4, -0.5, -5.1, -6.3, -4.8, -8.5, 6.2, -8.7]
                            },
                            "guide": {
                                "place_name": "Vancouver",
                                "region_code": "BC",
                                "tag_line": "Once You Step Into This Urban Paradise, You'll Never Want To Leave",
                                "main_image": "https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/vancouver_apartment_rentals_rental_housing_downtown.jpg",
                                "intro_images": ["https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/Vancouver_skyline_apartment_rental_rentals_house_rental_rentals_overcrowdi.jpg"],
                                "intro": "<p data-block-key=\"dblwc\">In the rest of Canada, everyone has a story about a friend who went out to Vancouver for a vacation and never came back. That’s because once you’ve stepped into this urban paradise, you’ll never want to leave. You might have to, though, because rents are higher than Vancouver skyscrapers. It’s too bad because everything else here is in harmony: natural beauty and urban conveniences, solid jobs but work/life balance, fun and peacefulness. The only thing out of whack is the huge demand for housing and the lack of supply, driving the prices up. But if you can afford your own cloud in this slice of heaven, it’s yours for the taking – and so worth it… even at these prices.</p>",
                                "sections": [{
                                    "title": "Housing Market",
                                    "body": "<p data-block-key=\"f8kpb\">By now, you’ve probably heard that the housing market in Vancouver is tough. So the question is: is it as bad as everyone claims? The short answer is… no. It’s worse. The city has declared that there’s a housing crisis, implementing new regulations around offshore ownership and short-term rentals in hopes of getting more units on the market. In spite of those steps, it’s almost impossible to find housing at affordable prices, so downtown Vancouver apartments for rent might be out of the question. What do you do about it? Step one, cry. Step two, cry again. Step three, make a plan. Give yourself plenty of time to locate and look at units, consider getting roommates, and ask for help from friends who live in the city. Don't be picky you might not be able to find pet-friendly rentals, so plan accordingly. With enough time and elbow grease, you’ll sort your housing situation out – and it’ll be worth all the work.</p><p data-block-key=\"fi2bh\"></p><p data-block-key=\"zzaz5\"></p><img src=\"https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/Vancouver_park_high_rise_apartments_rentals_rental.jpg\" alt=\"Vancouver park high rise apartments rentals rental.jpg\"/><p data-block-key=\"sdsfp\"></p><p data-block-key=\"w3kw4\"></p><p data-block-key=\"4sa9i\"><b>Typical housing type:</b></p><p data-block-key=\"4f2hc\">Apartment buildings of all sizes.</p><p data-block-key=\"t2sns\"></p><p data-block-key=\"kn5uh\"><b>Side note:</b></p><p data-block-key=\"kwuaz\">With the challenges in the Vancouver housing market, it may be worth getting a real estate agent to rent BC. Not only will an agent know all the tips and tricks for getting a deal, but they may have the connections to get you access to places that aren’t even on the market, and the best places to live Vancouver.</p>",
                                    "accordions": []
                                }, {
                                    "title": "Apartment Hunting",
                                    "body": "<p data-block-key=\"mmq0p\">Let’s point out the elephant in the room right off the bat… If you’re hunting for cheap rent, Vancouver is going to be a challenge. You’re pretty much limited to housing for students and shared places in rough neighbourhoods – and even then, finding apartments in Vancouver under $1,000 per month will be difficult.</p><p data-block-key=\"b1lsu\">As for all-inclusive Vancouver apartments to rent? They don’t exist, friends. Once you accept you’re going to be paying an arm and a leg though, you’ll have a good variety of options to choose from whether it be <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/1-bedrooms\"><b>1-bedroom</b></a> apartments for rent in Vancouver, or <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/2-bedrooms\"><b>2-bedroom</b></a> condos for rent in Vancouver, and even <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/3-bedrooms\"><b>3-bedroom</b></a> houses for rent in Vancouver to choose from. Realizing that cutting costs is hard actually frees up your options in Vancouver. Do you want granite countertops? <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/hardwood-flooring\"><b>Hardwood flooring</b></a><b>,</b> <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/ceramic-flooring\"><b>ceramic flooring</b></a><b>, or</b> <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/carpet-flooring\"><b>carpet flooring</b></a>? Overhead lighting? The city's properties have some of the largest variety of amenities in Canada. While amenities can raise prices even more, there are lots of places that are pet-friendly.</p>",
                                    "accordions": [{
                                        "title": "Explore Property Types",
                                        "description": "<p data-block-key=\"60uh5\">Canada’s West Coast is a sunny, warm, mountain paradise. It seems like everyone wants to live there, so we are sure you will find the right type of property that fits your needs.</p>",
                                        "panels": [{
                                            "title": "Apartments",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Apartment hunting in Vancouver can be stressful as the city is famous for its high prices. But that's for good reason, Vancouver is one of the most desirable places to live in Canada. Check out <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/apartments\"><b>Vancouver apartments for rent</b></a> to find your taste of the west coast lifestyle.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Basements",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">In Vancouver, a lot of homeowners will offset the cost of ownership by converting their basement into an apartment. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/basement\"><b>Vancouver basement apartments for rent</b></a> can be a great option for rent, but make sure the conversion is fully legal. A surprising amount of conversions are done without proper permits.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Townhouses",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Single family homes in Vancouver come at a hefty price tag. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/Vancouver/townhouse\"><b>Vancouver townhouses for rent</b></a> present a slightly more affordable option. Since you’ll be responsible for more of the property, ask the owner about maintenance responsibilities; a house falling apart will get annoying really fast.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Houses",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Having your own single family home in Vancouver is honestly the ultimate flex. Alternatively, a lot of <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/Vancouver/house\"><b>Vancouver houses for rent</b></a> are laneway houses which are basically a really bougie garage that has been converted to a living space. They are way more affordable and require less work than regular homes.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Rooms",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Unless you are prepared to spend big dollars for a place in Vancouver, sharing rent is a must. One of the best options for people looking to save a few bucks is to <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/private-room\"><b>find rooms for rent in Vancouver</b></a>. Be careful to find the roommates that are right for you. Anyone who has lived with a total slob before knows what we are talking about.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Condos",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"gj3k1\">Most of the available residential properties in downtown Vancouver are condos. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/condos\"><b>Vancouver condos for rent</b></a> can get you deep in the heart of Canada’s most desirable city. They won’t come cheap though so make a plan to budget your expenses from the get go. Affording groceries and food is kind of a necessity too.</p>"
                                        }]
                                    }, {
                                        "title": "Look for the Amenities you want",
                                        "description": "<p data-block-key=\"m0cst\">Living a positive lifestyle in Vancouver is easy. If you are ready to pay a premium, the cities diverse offerings are ready to be your new home</p>",
                                        "panels": [{
                                            "title": "Wheelchair Access",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">With all the new builds in the city, chances are you won’t have trouble finding options downtown. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/wheelchair-accessible\"><b>Vancouver wheelchair accessible apartments for rent</b></a> are easy to find with elevators, ramps, and ground level apartments to suit your needs.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Pool",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Sometimes you'll want to go for a swim but won’t feel like heading straight to the beach. Developers in Vancouver offer state of the art facilities for residents to enjoy. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/pool\"><b>Vancouver apartments for rent with a pool</b></a> are common and are a great way to meet your neighbours. Be friendly when going for a dip and you may just be invited to the next sushi night.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Gym",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Beautiful weather means beautiful people. Health and fitness is important in Vancouver so take advantage of <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/gym-fitness-center\"><b>Vancouver apartments with a gym</b></a> to get that year-round summer body.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Fireplace",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">The city rarely gets really cold so <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/fireplace\"><b>Vancouver apartments for rent with fireplaces</b></a> will likely be more decorative than functional. Be careful if it is an electric fireplace as hydro is notoriously expensive in Vancouver.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Dishwasher",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">If you are not taking advantage of some of Vancouver's world class seafood, then why are you even living there? <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/dishwasher\"><b>Vancouver apartments with a dishwasher</b></a> help with the clean-up after a good feast. Don’t run it too often though, British Columbia suffers from water shortages that can affect price and availability.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Balcony",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">The Vancouver skyline is incredible – where else can you look at mountains then turn around and look at the ocean? <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/balcony\"><b>Vancouver apartments for rent with a balcony</b></a> are everywhere and definitely worth a potential upcharge.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Air Conditioning",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">You know the stereotype that Canadians live in igloos? These people have never been to Vancouver. The weather is warm here, so with <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/air-conditioning\"><b>Vancouver apartments with air conditioning</b></a> you can expect to keep the air running a lot longer than normal. Be wary of hydro prices if it is a window or wall unit, but you can't really put a price on comfort anyways.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Washer and Dryer",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"2qh4k\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/washer-dryer\"><b>Vancouver apartments with a washer and dryer</b></a> are in no short supply. The high amount of new builds means that ensuite laundry can be found easily. But some buildings still have communal facilities. Ask the owner/manager about this when you tour.</p>"
                                        }]
                                    }, {
                                        "title": "Specialty Housing Filters",
                                        "description": "<p data-block-key=\"60uh5\">Housing in Vancouver is not as simple as just finding any old place and moving in. Rent is expensive so be sure to find the housing situation that fits your needs.</p>",
                                        "panels": [{
                                            "title": "Pet Friendly",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Vancouver has plenty of outdoor space to keep you and your pet happy. But if your little fur baby is a homebody check <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/pet-friendly\"><b>pet friendly rentals in Vancouver</b></a> and ask the owner/property manager about their policy. A noisy dog in a high density building may not be the best fit.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Furnished",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Vancouver draws a lot of people from overseas to the city. Coming from far away means you may struggle to bring furniture. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/furnished\"><b>Furnished apartments for rent in Vancouver</b></a> solve that problem. Check with the owner about quality and what exactly they offer. Chances are you will still need to buy a few more things.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Short-Term",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Moving to Vancouver for a temporary work term? <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/short-term\"><b>Short term rentals in Vancouver</b></a> can be found easily. Oftentimes it will be a sublet or lease transfer. So make sure to speak to potential roommates before signing anything. You want to make sure your lifestyles are compatible.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Corporate Housing",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">Vancouver is an economic hub, so you might find yourself relocating to the city for work. <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/corporate-housing\"><b>Vancouver corporate housing</b></a> is communities and buildings with professional friendly environments. Ask about available amenities and furnishings as they are common.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Student Housing",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">The University of British Columbia is one of the world's finest schools. Situated right in the heart of the city, <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/student-housing\"><b>Student Housing in Vancouver</b></a> is plentiful and in convenient locations. Tip – find a group of friends to live with. Sharing rent and utilities will make life way more affordable in Vancouver</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Affordable Housing",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"o2c05\">We don’t know what to tell you here, <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/cheap\"><b>cheap apartments for rent in Vancouver</b></a> are not the easiest to find. There are some neighbourhoods with decent prices, but practice caution when searching. A really low price in Vancouver probably means a significant drop in quality.</p>"
                                        }, {
                                            "title": "Luxury Rentals",
                                            "body": "<p data-block-key=\"gj3k1\">Vancouver is beautiful and so are the properties. Hardwood floors, new appliances, great views are commonplace. If you have the resources, why not enjoy Vancouver to its full potential. Check out <a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/luxury\"><b>luxury apartments in Vancouver</b></a> for your taste of the high life.</p>"
                                        }]
                                    }]
                                }, {
                                    "title": "Residents",
                                    "body": "<p data-block-key=\"sfol4\">With a forest, ocean and mountains all just a stone’s throw away, Vancouver draws outdoorsy folks. Locals tend to be passionate about outdoor sports, as well as general health and fitness. Nutrition is highly prized, with plant-based diets being common. Vancouver is a highly diverse city, with over half the population speaking multiple languages. The community is welcoming to both immigrants and refugees. This should come as no surprise as Vancouverites tend to be progressive and active regarding socio-political issues. There is, however, a significant financial divide between the wealthiest locals – who earn well over $100,000 – and the poorest – who struggle with homelessness.</p><p data-block-key=\"9uwl9\"></p><p data-block-key=\"uw6qv\"><b>Perfect for:</b></p><p data-block-key=\"39yuf\">Progressive outdoor lovers.</p><p data-block-key=\"mrw8o\"></p><p data-block-key=\"r4svw\"><b>Not-so-perfect for:</b></p><p data-block-key=\"5ziz1\">Alt-righters.</p><p data-block-key=\"6lnn9\"></p><p data-block-key=\"j42ld\"></p><img src=\"https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/Vancouver_park_lake_tourist_parks_nature_tourism_camping.jpg\" alt=\"Vancouver park lake tourist parks nature tourism camping.jpg\"/><p data-block-key=\"3a56p\"></p><p data-block-key=\"2ck1x\"></p>",
                                    "accordions": []
                                }, {
                                    "title": "Neighbourhood",
                                    "body": "<p data-block-key=\"w5c9d\">Vancouver is known for having Stanley Park in the middle of the city. There’s also the Pacific Ocean at the city’s edge – and the Coast Mountains just outside the area. Outdoor sports and activities are all around the city and surrounding area. In terms of food, there are plenty of restaurant options, but seafood is one of the local specialities. There are also a number of farmers’ markets if you’re looking for fresh produce or fish. Don’t forget to hit main neighbourhoods, like Gastown, to catch a shoot of one of your favourite TV shows or movies (read: Deadpool 2)! For a night out, head to Granville Street. You can also go to Granville Island if a relaxing afternoon is more your speed. There are a good variety of private and public schools in the area, as well as UBC, BCIT and Simon Fraser. Don’t forget to check out the art gallery, which is spectacular!</p><p data-block-key=\"ahpiw\"></p><p data-block-key=\"yc80l\"></p><img src=\"https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/Vancouver_water_sunset_sunrise_photography_downtown.jpg\" alt=\"Vancouver water sunset sunrise photography downtown.jpg\"/><p data-block-key=\"pc17w\"></p><p data-block-key=\"j8dyx\"></p><p data-block-key=\"rnubn\"><b>Landmarks:</b></p><p data-block-key=\"m2dbb\">Stanley Park</p><p data-block-key=\"jn52l\">Granville Island</p><p data-block-key=\"662qs\">Vancouver Aquarium</p><p data-block-key=\"7jslx\">Vancouver City Hall</p><p data-block-key=\"06v3i\">Brockton Point Totem Pole</p><p data-block-key=\"d4sin\">Waterfront Station</p><p data-block-key=\"7bj8h\">A-maze-ing Laughter</p><p data-block-key=\"ckrgn\">Library Square</p><p data-block-key=\"gkdlb\">Vancouver Lookout</p><p data-block-key=\"zm5cg\">Lions Gate Bridge</p><p data-block-key=\"4gtaq\">Gastown Steam Clock</p><p data-block-key=\"s8zki\">Robson Street</p><p data-block-key=\"pd9vb\">Chinatown</p><p data-block-key=\"mt9x6\"></p><img src=\"https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/vancouver_water_attraction_tourism_event.jpg\" alt=\"vancouver water attraction tourism event.jpg\"/><p data-block-key=\"2yaz1\">Find Vancouver apartments for rent in these popular neighbourhoods:</p><p data-block-key=\"5ujof\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/kitsilano\">Kitsilano, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"93ssb\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/west-point-grey\">West Point Grey, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"bat2r\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/strathcona\">Strathcona, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"cdhq3\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/south-granville\">South Granville, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"4gkgs\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/killarney\">Killarney, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"1fget\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/hastings-sunrise\">Hastings-Sunrise, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"at2cf\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/grandview-woodland\">Grandview-Woodland, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"ddomc\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/sunset\">Sunset, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"74uka\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/kerrisdale\">Kerrisdale, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"e1rqk\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/mount-pleasant\">Mount Pleasant, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"7f21j\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/fairview\">Fairview, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"549pl\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/yaletown\">Yaletown, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"elljf\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/coal-harbour\">Coal Harbour, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"9u1rs\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/marpole\">Marpole, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"7a4a0\"><a href=\"https://rentals.ca/vancouver/downtown\">Downtown, Vancouver, BC</a></p><p data-block-key=\"dab7j\"></p>",
                                    "accordions": []
                                }, {
                                    "title": "Life & Style",
                                    "body": "<p data-block-key=\"bt14o\">Vancouver is all about work/life balance. Even those who love their work aren’t consumed by it, setting aside time for health, fitness, communing with nature, and connecting with loved ones. Taking time off to kick back and have fun is also seen as important. During the week, that kicking back could be as simple as taking a walk in Stanley Park or grabbing dinner with friends at a local hotspot. On weekends, though, things get more elaborate as locals often head off on adventures or pop into the mountains to hit the slopes. Basically, Vancouver is all about making your #lifegoals a reality IRL.</p><p data-block-key=\"7z099\"></p><p data-block-key=\"a943i\"></p><img src=\"https://images.rentals.ca/original_images/vancouver_dolphin_jump_seaworld_amusement_park_community_downtown.jpg\" alt=\"vancouver dolphin jump seaworld amusement park community downtown.jpg\"/><p data-block-key=\"l7xs5\"></p><p data-block-key=\"f5q0w\"></p>",
                                    "accordions": []
                                }]
